hema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a64159c3e2e91cc647771aff7d14e375ae00e6c7e84a948d6ea81ecf01867cf6","file":"preprints/Single-Exponential-Recovery-and-Bounded-Price-Strictness-for-Metric-k-Median-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":142,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"7ee20b355b199d30cbad454d30fd087ff2733b35f983b0060fa24ea77383a90b","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Single-Exponential-Recovery-and-Bounded-Price-Strictness-for-Metric-k-Median-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a64159c3e2e91cc647771aff7d14e375ae00e6c7e84a948d6ea81ecf01867cf6","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Single-Exponential-Recovery-and-Bounded-Price-Strictness-for-Metric-k-Median-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L142"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{main:theorem}\nThere is an absolute constant $\\sigma>0$ with the following property.\nFor every fixed $a>0$, a randomized polynomial-time algorithm for metric\n$k$-median always returns a set $S\\subseteq F$ with $|S|\\le k$ and satisfies\n\\[\n \\Pr\\!\\left\\{\\operatorname{cost}(S)\n       \\le(2-\\sigma)\\operatorname{opt}_k\\right\\}\n \\ge 1-(|D|+|F|+2)^{-a}.\n\\]\nThe same algorithm can be chosen to satisfy\n$\\mathbb E\\operatorname{cost}(S)\\le(2-\\sigma)\\operatorname{opt}_k$.\nThe running time is polynomial in the bit length of the finite rational\nmetric input. Its degree may depend on the fixed constants."}
